From: =?UTF-8?q?Yank=C4=B1=20K=C3=BC=C3=A7=C3=BCk?=
 <kendinikertenkelebek@me.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:05:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] feat(specfile): accept sha256sum for source archives

Source archives could only be verified with SHA-1 (sha1sum, mandatory),
which is no longer collision resistant. Recipes can now give sha256sum,
sha1sum or both; at least one is required and every hash that is given
must match.

- specfile.Archive: sha1sum and sha256sum are both optional attributes; a
  decode hook rejects an archive with neither; hashes() returns the
  (algorithm, digest) pairs to check, sha256 first.
- sourcearchive.SourceArchive.hashes_match() checks all of them, both for
  the cached archive and before unpacking.
- util: hash_file(filename, algorithm) backs sha1_file(), the new
  sha256_file() and check_file_hash(), which keeps sha1 as its default so
  other callers are unchanged.
- pisi-spec.dtd and pisi-spec.rng: sha1sum becomes optional and sha256sum
  is added; the RelaxNG rule requires at least one of them. (The full
  RelaxNG schema already rejected current recipes before this change, for
  example on empty <Patches>; the Archive rule was checked on its own.)

Existing recipes keep working unchanged; moving them to sha256sum is a
separate, mechanical change in core and main.

Tests: tests/archivehashtest.py (6 tests: sha1 only, sha256 only, both,
neither rejected, file hashing, SourceArchive matching) passes with
Python 2.7 in pisilinux/chroot; the other test modules give the same
results as on master. Integration with this PiSi in the chroot: which
builds with sha256sum only and with both hashes, a wrong sha256sum stops
the build with "check_file_hash failed", and "pisi index" keeps the
sha256sum attribute in the generated index.
